an ordinary report     qbr-2024-Q3.pdf
   pages 1   pypdf  1,476 chars   pdfplumber  1,476 chars   tables found 0
   first lines: ['Meridian Supply Co. — Quarterly Business Review', '2024 Q3']

a two-column page      01-newsletter-two-column.pdf
   pages 1   pypdf    675 chars   pdfplumber    664 chars   tables found 0
   first lines: ['Meridian Monthly — December 2025', 'From the Managing Director']

a scan                 06-goods-received-note-SCANNED.pdf
   pages 1   pypdf      0 chars   pdfplumber      0 chars   tables found 0
   first lines: ['']

Three documents, three different problems.

The ordinary report extracts cleanly, and the table inside it comes out as
text — the columns become a run of numbers with the alignment gone. Chapter 10
showed what that does once it is chunked.

The two-column page extracts in the wrong order. Both columns are read as one
stream, so a sentence from the left column is followed by an unrelated sentence
from the right. It is fluent, plausible, and not what the page says.

The scan extracts nothing at all. Zero characters. There is no text layer to
find, because there is no text — only an image of some. This is the failure
that produces an empty index and a search that returns nothing, with no error
anywhere in the pipeline.
